            "review_text": "Julia M\nAldgate, Australia15 contributions\n0\nLove this little hideout\nJul 2019 • Couples\nMy husband and I have been here a few times now as we've enjoyed the dishes we've eaten and it's next to ben tahn market where we are daily. The coconuts are always cold and served with a cute curly straw, the service is always nice (they come over when you need them to but leave you alone otherwise) and the food is great. We've had pho, bahn mi roasted pork, Vietnamese pancake and the bowl with meat and noodles and beans. It's always super tasty and usually about 200,000 VD for both of us combined for food, water or beer and a meal.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 8, 2019",
